  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Hybridisation is found by steric number which is generally&nbsp;the summation of sigma bonds and lone pairs of electrons.</p><p>So as we can see&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></math>&nbsp;has four sigma bonds so it has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">b</mi><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">c</mi></math>&nbsp;has three sigma bonds so it has&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation.</p>"
  }
